Maintainer: T. Sophia Luo <lutiffan@umich.edu>
Description: Identification of CpG sites with multimodal DNA methylation 
  distributions, which can be caused by biological variation or technical 
  artifacts, is an important quality control step when analyzing whole genome 
  methylation data. MethylModes is a computationally efficient, peak detection 
  algorithm implemented in a Shiny application and easily incorporated into 
  existing analytic pipelines for large-scale epigenetic studies.
